\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Piecewise-linear interpolation of the non-linear matter power spectrum \(P_{\delta \delta }[(\ell +1/2)/\chi ,\, z(\chi )]\) as a function of comoving distance for four representative multipoles (\(\ell = 10\), \(100\), \(1000\), and \(10\,000\); top-left to bottom-right). In each panel, the upper sub-panel compares the power spectrum evaluated by \texttt  {CCL} (solid) with four interpolation schemes identified in the legend: first-order numerical interpolation, second-order numerical interpolation, third-order numerical interpolation, and the \texttt  {LimberCloud} piecewise-linear scheme. The lower sub-panel shows the ratio of each scheme to \texttt  {CCL}; dashed lines mark the \(\pm 1\%\) level.\relax }}{10}{figure.caption.4}\protected@file@percent }
